&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Horizon Trading Solutions is an independent global technology company focused on electronic trading, supporting agency and principal business activities across equities and derivatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 20 years, we have equipped leading capital market participants with algorithmic trading technology and direct connectivity to more than 80 exchanges worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently looking for an Account Manager EMEA to strengthen to drive sustainable revenue growth and increase the value of Horizon’s existing client accounts by developing structured account plans, identifying upsell and cross-sell opportunities, securing renewals and strengthening relationships with key decision-makers. The Account Manager acts as the commercial owner of each account and coordinates internal teams to turn client knowledge into profitable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;1. Grow the Existing Client Portfolio&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage an account plan for each priority account, covering growth potential, stakeholder mapping, key challenges, competition, opportunities and actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, qualify and convert upsell, cross-sell, geographic expansion and functional expansion opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a reliable, documented expansion pipeline and keep it regularly updated in the CRM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare business cases and commercial proposals, and lead negotiations and contracting through to closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;2. Secure Retention and Renewals&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate renewals and churn risks, with a retention plan shared with the relevant teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor product usage, client satisfaction, value delivered and commercial pain points across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead account reviews and executive business reviews, providing actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;3. Build Executive Relationships&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build lasting relationships with sponsors and decision-makers across business, IT, trading, operations and procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand each client’s strategy, organisation and priorities in order to develop new use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the client internally while protecting Horizon’s commercial interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;4. Coordinate Internal Execution&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate Client Services, Customer Delivery, Product, PreSales, Legal and Finance around the account objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure clear handovers and follow through on commitments made to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share market signals, client needs and competitive insights that can inform the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;5. Manage Performance&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track growth, retention, pipeline, forecast, stakeholder coverage and margin indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce evidence-based forecasts, explain variances and recommend corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to commercial discipline, sales methodologies and the team’s continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Expected Outcomes Within 12 Months&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% of priority accounts have an approved account plan that is updated quarterly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achievement of the annual recurring revenue and/or revenue expansion target across the assigned portfolio (quantified target to be defined).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A qualified expansion pipeline maintained at a level consistent with the annual objective (recommended benchmark: at least 3x the target).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Renewal rate and net revenue retention in line with agreed objectives, with no strategic renewal identified too late.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-threaded mapping of decision-makers and influencers across all strategic accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable monthly forecast, up-to-date CRM data, and clearly documented risks and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 24pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least five years of experience in account management, sales or complex B2B business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in finance or capital markets is mandatory: investment banking, brokerage, asset management, fintech, financial software or a comparable environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable results in growing existing accounts, complex negotiations and managing long sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage effectively with both business and technical stakeholders, including at executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of SaaS/licensing models, recurring revenue, renewals and account profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to trading technology, software platforms, APIs/connectivity or IT projects would be a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in French and English is essential; another European language would be an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Skills and Behaviours&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset and results orientation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of financial markets and understanding of client challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account planning and prioritisation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing, active listening and relationship-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial negotiation and value-based selling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional collaboration and strong execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM discipline, forecasting and data-driven management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technological curiosity, autonomy and an entrepreneurial mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Horizon is an equal opportunity employer. We promote diversity, multiculturalism, and inclusion.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who/What is Artefact?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Artefact is a next-generation strategy and data consulting firm dedicated to transforming&amp;nbsp;organizations through data and AI. We combine the rigor of top-tier strategy consulting&amp;nbsp;with deep expertise in data, digital, and analytics to help clients achieve tangible&lt;br&gt;business impact.&lt;br&gt;With 1,800+ consultants, data scientists, and engineers across 23 countries, we work&amp;nbsp;with global leaders such as Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange, and Sanofi. Our Zurich office is&amp;nbsp;at the heart of Artefact’s growth, advising clients on their most pressing strategic&amp;nbsp;challenges — from AI strategy and governance to digital transformation roadmaps and&amp;nbsp;new business model design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We are looking for a Senior Data &amp;amp; AI Architect who combines business strategy and technology across Data and GenAI. You will design the operating model and the organization of the Data &amp;amp; GenAI CoE, define the target architecture, and steer data products from demand through to rollout.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Operating model and organization&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design the Data &amp;amp; AI operating model (centralized, federated, hub-and-spoke) following Data Mesh principles: roles, responsibilities, domain ownership and governance mechanisms.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Define the organization of the Data &amp;amp; GenAI CoE: scope, service catalogue, skills, sizing and engagement model with business domains.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design end-to-end processes for demand management, use case prioritization, funding and value tracking.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Architecture and technology choices&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Define the target data platform architecture on cloud (Azure, AWS, GCP) and Databricks, including GenAI components (RAG, agents, vector stores, LLMOps).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Run make-or-buy analyses and vendor selections: scouting, evaluation criteria, business case, TCO and final recommendation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Check that architecture, security and data governance choices are consistent with enterprise standards and with the operating model.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Data products: from demand to rollout&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Gather and formalize functional requirements with the business, translating them into data products with owners, consumers, SLAs and quality metrics.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Design data products from both a functional angle (use cases, KPIs, impacted processes) and a technical one (data model, pipelines, interfaces, serving layer).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Act as design authority during implementation: review system integrator solutions and oversee quality, progress and risks of the rollout.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At least 4 years of professional experience in IT.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At least 2 years on projects focused on AI/GenAI, Data Mesh and functional requirements gathering.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Consulting experience, ideally in strategy consulting, combined with experience at a system integrator or delivery firm.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Hands-on experience designing operating models, Data/AI organizations or CoEs.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience with make-or-buy analyses, vendor selection or target architecture definition.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Excellent written and spoken English.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Technical and functional skills:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;You will not be expected to write code, but you need to know the technologies well enough to assess them, challenge vendors and spot a flawed setup.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Data Mesh and governance: domain ownership, data products, federated governance, data contracts, catalogues and lineage (e.g. Unity Catalog, OpenMetadata, Collibra).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cloud: data and AI PaaS services on at least one of Azure, AWS and GCP; security, networking and FinOps principles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Databricks: Lakehouse, Delta Lake, Unity Catalog, Workflows; ability to assess design and cost.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;GenAI: RAG and agentic architectures, LLMOps, model evaluation, platforms such as Azure AI Foundry, Vertex AI and Bedrock.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Operating model: Data/AI organization, CoE, roles (data owner, data steward, product owner), demand and portfolio processes.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Requirements and delivery: requirements gathering, user stories, process modelling, agile methods, programme governance.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Business: business cases, TCO, value tracking, and the ability to translate technical choices into economic impact.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;German not strictly required.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience with clients in pharma sector.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Cloud or Databricks certifications (e.g. Azure Solutions Architect, Databricks Data Engineer or Solutions Architect).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience in tech due diligence or post-merger transformation projects.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Prior technical background as an engineer or developer.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;A role bridging strategy and technology, with direct impact on client decisions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;International projects on Data Mesh, data platforms and GenAI.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Close collaboration with the Project Lead and a growth path towards programme leadership roles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Location and working model: (Hybrid) Zurich or Lausanne.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive compensation package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in &lt;strong&gt;Zürich&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don’t worry if you don’t meet all the criteria! We value motivation, pragmatic problem-solving, and potential above all else. We’d love to hear from you and learn more about your passion for driving the AI revolution.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
